  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: A quiet weather pattern is expected through the \nweek, with temperatures moderating to near normal beginning\nMonday.\n\nBottom line: No hazardous weather is expected through this \nweek.\n\nHigh pressure will maintain control of the weather pattern \nacross the Mid-Atlantic this week, supporting mostly clear \nskies and windflow generally from the north-northeast. Latest \ndata continues to indicate low pressure developing off the \nAtlantic coast will remain far enough east so as not to have \nsignificant impact on weather conditions across our area. \n\nStill forecasting Monday early morning temperatures to range \nfrom the upper 20s to the mid 30s across the mountains and \nfoothills, which will support another round of frost that may \ndamage or kill sensitive vegetation. Thereafter, temperatures \nwill gradually moderate to near-normal for the remainder of the \nweek.",
